@@ -240,3 +240,37 @@ python -I tools/psocache_usersig.py <cache> [--entry N] [--limit N] [--json]
 
 It reuses the parser from `tools/psocache_inspect.py`, prints the aggregate over the first `--limit` graphics PSOs
 (all by default) or one PSO with `--entry N`, and never prints a hash.
+
+## Runtime Vulkan pipeline cache
+
+The Vulkan backend uses the same device cache for graphics pipelines from slot 57 and for compute pipelines from
+slots 62 and 67. The hardware driver compiles each new combination of translated shaders, pipeline layout and
+pipeline state. A later launch can reuse the driver's compiled result. The first launch still pays for misses.
+
+By default the session file is `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Leonida\pipeline_cache.user.bin`. The runtime reads the
+`translation_sources.sha256` written by the shaders stage under the configured translated shader directory.
+A missing or malformed fingerprint disables the session file for that device. Regenerating the shaders with
+`make_game.py` produces the marker for older work folders. Vulkan continues to use its in-memory cache.
+
+| Setting | Behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| `LEONIDA_PIPELINE_CACHE` | Set to `off` to disable session loads and writes, or to a filename in an existing work or cache directory. Paths inside the configured game directory and paths that alias the build seed are refused. |
+| `LEONIDA_PIPELINE_CACHE_SAVE_SECONDS` | Minimum time between checkpoint attempts after a successful pipeline creation. Defaults to 120 seconds. Set to 0 to save only at device teardown. |
+| `LEONIDA_PIPELINE_CACHE_MAX_MB` | Maximum session payload in MiB, default 1024. Vulkan snapshots the entire cache, including its seed. When a seed already exceeds the cap, persisting additions requires a cap above the combined size and sufficient memory and disk space. |
+
+A session file contains a versioned header, payload length and checksum, the Vulkan driver version and the
+translator fingerprint. Its Vulkan payload header must also match the vendor ID, device ID and pipeline cache
+UUID. The runtime falls back to the read-only offline seed `pipeline_cache.bin` beside the executable if the
+session file is stale, corrupt or incompatible, then to an empty cache if the seed is unavailable or rejected.
+A newer or newly rebuilt seed takes precedence. The runtime serializes writers, merges compatible intervening
+saves and replaces the file by renaming a completed staging file in the same directory.
+
+A checkpoint runs on the pipeline-creating thread and can take time for large files. A forced exit retains
+completed checkpoints. For a boot comparison, use the same runtime, translated shaders, device and driver in
+both runs. Record loaded and saved bytes, driver-reported application-cache hits, the time to the first visible
+frame and the number of completed draws at a fixed elapsed time. A file load alone does not establish a hit.
+
+The synthetic tests `d3d12_pipeline_cache_persist` and `d3d12_pipeline_cache_persist_periodic` cover fresh-process
+compute hits, invalidation, protected paths and checkpointing before teardown. To measure graphics, run
+`d3d12_slot57_draw_test --cache-file <scratch-file>` twice with the same initially absent path. Each run validates
+nine pixel probes and prints the number of creations, valid feedback records, cache hits and driver time.
